      "schoolName": "TRƯỜNG THCS ĐỒNG YÊN",
      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_7_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 1 (Hội thoại - 1 Giọng Nữ, 1 Giọng Nam):\nLan (Giọng Nữ):\tHi Mark, what do you usually do in your spare time?\nMark (Giọng Nam):\tHello Lan! I enjoy doing origami and planting flowers in the garden.\nLan (Giọng Nữ):\tDoes gardening help you feel relaxed after studying?\nMark (Giọng Nam):\tYes, it keeps me close to nature and helps reduce study stress.\nLan (Giọng Nữ):\tAre you joining our school's Green Sunday club this weekend?\nMark (Giọng Nam):\tOf course! We will clean the town park and collect plastic bottles for recycling.\n\n🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 2 (Độc thoại):\nCommunity service brings tremendous benefits to both volunteers and society. Last winter, our youth volunteer group organized a warm clothing donation program called Winter Warmth. Over three hundred students donated thick jackets, warm wool blankets, and storybooks. We delivered these essential gifts directly to poor children living in remote highland villages in Ha Giang. Seeing their radiant smiles made all of us feel immense joy and happiness.",
      "writingRubric": "1. Mở đoạn (Topic sentence): 0.25đ\n2. Phát triển ý (Supporting sentences): 0.25đ\n3. Vốn từ vựng & cấu trúc ngữ pháp phong phú: 0.25đ\n4. Độ chính xác chính tả & ngữ pháp: 0.25đ. Tổng: 1.0 điểm.",
      "sampleWritingText": "Community service plays an essential role in improving our local neighborhood. Every weekend, our youth club joins the Green Sunday campaign to clean streets, pick up plastic litter around lakes, and plant flowering trees. These activities not only protect our living environment but also teach us valuable lessons about teamwork, social responsibility, and caring for others.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nCommunity service provides teenagers with valuable opportunities to support their local community. Last weekend, our secondary school youth union launched a voluntary program named Green Weekend'. Over two hundred students volunteered to pick up plastic litter, clean the park lake, and plant young (23) ________ along walking paths. We also collected used textbooks and warm clothes to (24) ________ to underprivileged children living in remote mountainous hamlets. Participating in such volunteer projects not only makes our neighbourhood cleaner (25) ________ also teaches young students essential life skills like teamwork, empathy, and social (26) ________. Everyone felt deeply proud to contribute to the (27) ________ of society.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nBirdwatching, also known as birding, is one of the most enriching outdoor hobbies enjoyed by millions of nature enthusiasts globally. All you need to embark on this hobby is a lightweight pair of binoculars, a field identification handbook, and a keen sense of observation. Birdwatching encourages people to spend more time outdoors in natural habitats like lush national parks, serene wetlands, and river estuaries. While searching for elusive bird species, observers walk along forest trails, breathing fresh crisp air and getting gentle aerobic exercise. Furthermore, identifying birds by their plumage colors, flight patterns, and melodic songs sharpens cognitive alertness and patience. Birdwatchers also contribute directly to global wildlife conservation. Many hobbyists log their daily sightings into scientific databases like eBird, helping professional ornithologists track bird migration routes and monitor endangered bird populations threatened by climate change.",
