          "passage": "Winters in the northern highlands of Lao Cai are notoriously harsh, with temperatures frequently plunging near freezing point. Many ethnic minority schoolchildren in highland hamlets lack adequate winter clothing to stay warm on their long walks to school. In response, our student union spearheaded the Warmth for the Highlands' winter donation drive, amassing over eight hundred woollen coats, insulated boots, and thick blankets. Our volunteer convoy navigated treacherous mountain passes to deliver the relief supplies directly to schools. Witnessing the children bundle up warmly filled our hearts with immense gratitude and fraternal love."
