      "audioScript": "🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 1 (Hội thoại - 1 Giọng Nữ, 1 Giọng Nam):\nLan (Giọng Nữ):\tHi Mark, what do you usually do in your spare time?\nMark (Giọng Nam):\tHello Lan! I enjoy doing origami and planting flowers in the garden.\nLan (Giọng Nữ):\tDoes gardening help you feel relaxed after studying?\nMark (Giọng Nam):\tYes, it keeps me close to nature and helps reduce study stress.\nLan (Giọng Nữ):\tAre you joining our school's Green Sunday club this weekend?\nMark (Giọng Nam):\tOf course! We will clean the town park and collect plastic bottles for recycling.\n\n🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 2 (Độc thoại):\nCommunity service brings tremendous benefits to both volunteers and society. Last winter, our youth volunteer group organized a warm clothing donation program called Winter Warmth. Over three hundred students donated thick jackets, warm wool blankets, and storybooks. We delivered these essential gifts directly to poor children living in remote highland villages in Ha Giang. Seeing their radiant smiles made all of us feel immense joy and happiness.",
      "writingRubric": "1. Mở đoạn (Topic sentence): 0.25đ\n2. Phát triển ý (Supporting sentences): 0.25đ\n3. Vốn từ vựng & cấu trúc ngữ pháp phong phú: 0.25đ\n4. Độ chính xác chính tả & ngữ pháp: 0.25đ. Tổng: 1.0 điểm.",
      "sampleWritingText": "Community service plays an essential role in improving our local neighborhood. Every weekend, our youth club joins the Green Sunday campaign to clean streets, pick up plastic litter around lakes, and plant flowering trees. These activities not only protect our living environment but also teach us valuable lessons about teamwork, social responsibility, and caring for others.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nLast Saturday, our school cooperated with the provincial blood transfusion center to host a voluntary blood donation day. Hundreds of teachers, parents, and older youths queued up enthusiastically in the school gymnasium. Medical personnel performed health screenings before safely collecting units of blood. Each donated unit of blood can save up to three lives in emergency surgical procedures. Although secondary students are too young to donate blood, we assisted by serving warm sweet milk, handing out certificates, and cheering donors.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nMastering an acoustic musical instrument requires a disciplined synthesis of physical coordination, auditory sensitivity, and emotional expression. Classical guitarists must spend months developing fingertip calluses, memorizing complex chord progressions, and mastering polyphonic fingerpicking. When playing in an ensemble, musicians learn to listen attentively to their peers, synchronizing tempos and balancing acoustic dynamics. Music education enriches neural development, enhances emotional empathy, and provides teenagers with a lifelong vehicle for profound artistic fulfillment.",
