      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_8_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 1 (Hội thoại - 1 Giọng Nam, 1 Giọng Nữ):\nNam (Giọng Nam):\tHi Mai, what do you usually do to unwind after strenuous school hours?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tHello Nam! I fancy making origami crafts and helping my mother cultivate vegetables in the garden.\nNam (Giọng Nam):\tDo you participate in any school clubs?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tYes, I am an active member of our school's IT and English Speaking Club.\nNam (Giọng Nam):\tHow does joining the club benefit your studies?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tIt helps me improve my presentation skills and cope effectively with academic pressure.\n\n🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 2 (Độc thoại):\nLife in the Vietnamese countryside offers a harmonious rhythm that contrasts sharply with the frantic pace of major metropolises. During the golden harvest season, the vast paddy fields stretch like boundless carpets of ripe rice under the radiant sunlight. Local farmers work diligently from early dawn, harvesting golden stalks and loading grain carts. In the evening, the peaceful village echoes with children's laughter as they fly paper kites on grassy dikes or cycle along winding riverbanks. The close-knit camaraderie among villagers creates a safe, caring, and tranquil living environment.",
      "writingRubric": "1. Mở đoạn (Topic sentence): 0.25đ\n2. Phát triển ý (Supporting sentences): 0.25đ\n3. Vốn từ vựng & cấu trúc ngữ pháp phong phú: 0.25đ\n4. Độ chính xác chính tả & ngữ pháp: 0.25đ. Tổng: 1.0 điểm.",
      "sampleWritingText": "Life in the countryside provides many memorable experiences and benefits. The air is always fresh, peaceful, and unpolluted compared to busy cities. People live closely together, showing great hospitality and mutual support. In addition, teenagers in rural villages often enjoy outdoor activities like flying kites on grassy dikes, swimming in clear rivers, and riding bicycles around village lanes.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nAdolescence is a pivotal stage of life marked by rapid emotional and intellectual development. However, modern teenagers frequently experience intense stress stemming from rigorous academic expectations and peer (23) ________. Constantly comparing personal performance with others on social media can erode self-esteem and provoke persistent anxiety. To maintain good mental well-being, teenagers should learn how to manage their time (24) ________ and set realistic goals. Engaging in daily physical exercise, cultivating creative hobbies, and getting sufficient sleep help relieve nervous tension. Most importantly, teenagers should openly (25) ________ their worries with caring parents, teachers, or counselors instead of keeping them (26) ________ inside. Cultivating emotional resilience allows youths to overcome difficulties with (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe ubiquity of smartphones and social media platforms has revolutionized teenage socialization, but it has also given rise to a perilous challenge: cyberbullying. Unlike traditional schoolyard bullying which ends when the bell rings, cyberbullying can pursue victims relentlessly twenty-four hours a day. Cyberbullying takes various malicious forms, including posting humiliating rumors, sharing private photographs without consent, and sending threatening instant messages. Because perpetrators can conceal their identities behind anonymous accounts, they often act with greater cruelty. Victims frequently suffer from severe sleep disruption, academic decline, social isolation, and chronic depression. To shield teenagers from digital hazards, schools and parents must take proactive measures. Students should be taught digital citizenship, emphasizing that words typed behind screens carry real consequences. If subjected to online harassment, teenagers should never retaliate; instead, they should save evidence, block the perpetrator, and report the abuse immediately to trusted adults.",
