          "passage": "The ubiquity of smartphones and social media platforms has revolutionized teenage socialization, but it has also given rise to a perilous challenge: cyberbullying. Unlike traditional schoolyard bullying which ends when the bell rings, cyberbullying can pursue victims relentlessly twenty-four hours a day. Cyberbullying takes various malicious forms, including posting humiliating rumors, sharing private photographs without consent, and sending threatening instant messages. Because perpetrators can conceal their identities behind anonymous accounts, they often act with greater cruelty. Victims frequently suffer from severe sleep disruption, academic decline, social isolation, and chronic depression. To shield teenagers from digital hazards, schools and parents must take proactive measures. Students should be taught digital citizenship, emphasizing that words typed behind screens carry real consequences. If subjected to online harassment, teenagers should never retaliate; instead, they should save evidence, block the perpetrator, and report the abuse immediately to trusted adults."
