      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_9_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 1 (Hội thoại - 1 Giọng Nam, 1 Giọng Nữ):\nTom (Giọng Nam):\tHi Mai! Where did you go last weekend with your class?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tHello Tom! We had a wonderful field trip to Bat Trang pottery village near Ha Noi.\nTom (Giọng Nam):\tBat Trang? That sounds exciting! Did you try making any pottery yourself?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tYes! A local artisan guided us on how to mold wet clay on a spinning wheel to make a small bowl.\nTom (Giọng Nam):\tWas it difficult to shape the clay?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tIt required patience and steady hands, but it was so much fun. Crafting pottery helped me unwind and appreciate traditional handicrafts.\n\n🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 2 (Độc thoại):\nDa Nang is widely celebrated as one of the most livable, modern, and beautiful cities in Viet Nam. Situated along the scenic central coast, the city combines stunning natural landscapes such as the Marble Mountains and Son Tra Peninsula with modern public infrastructure. The local government maintains clean streets, efficient electric bus transit, and beautiful sandy beaches. Furthermore, iconic landmarks like the Dragon Bridge, which breathes fire and water on weekend evenings, make Da Nang an attractive destination for visitors.",
      "writingRubric": "1. Mở đoạn (Topic sentence): 0.25đ\n2. Phát triển ý (Supporting sentences): 0.25đ\n3. Vốn từ vựng & cấu trúc ngữ pháp phong phú: 0.25đ\n4. Độ chính xác chính tả & ngữ pháp: 0.25đ. Tổng: 1.0 điểm.",
      "sampleWritingText": "Preserving traditional craft villages is of great importance for our cultural heritage. Bat Trang pottery village and Van Phuc silk village are vivid symbols of Vietnamese craftsmanship and history. Traditional crafts provide stable livelihoods for local artisans and attract tourists from all over the world. We should support local craft products and introduce them to international friends.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nAdolescence is often accompanied by significant physical and emotional changes. Today, teenagers frequently experience (23) ________ from heavy school workloads and extracurricular expectations. To overcome this challenge, mental health experts advise students to manage their time (24) ________. Instead of staying up late reviewing lessons, teenagers should establish a fixed sleep schedule and take short breaks during study sessions. Regular physical exercise, such as jogging, swimming, or cycling, releases endorphins that reduce anxiety. Moreover, having open conversations with parents, teachers, or trusted friends can help teens (25) ________ solutions to their personal difficulties. A well-balanced diet rich in vitamins and minerals is also (26) ________ for maintaining sustained cognitive energy. Remember that asking for assistance is never a sign of weakness, but a wise decision to (27) ________ mental and physical well-being.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nIn the modern era, more than half of the world's population resides in urban environments, a proportion expected to climb steeply in the coming decades. This rapid urbanization places tremendous stress on energy grids, water supplies, and public services. To address these complex issues, urban designers are pioneering the concept of eco-smart cities', which combine cutting-edge green technologies with citizen-centered infrastructure. In an eco-smart metropolis, digital sensors placed across buildings and streets monitor energy consumption, atmospheric conditions, and real-time traffic volume. Street lamps automatically dim when roads are vacant, saving valuable electricity. Rooftops are routinely transformed into community gardens or solar power stations, which cool interior temperatures and generate clean renewable power. Rainwater is harvested through smart drainage systems to nourish public parks and clean street walkways. Nevertheless, the transformation into a smart city is not without its difficulties. Initial construction costs are substantial, requiring partnerships between government agencies and technology firms. Additionally, municipal leaders must ensure that low-income citizens have equal access to digital public services so that technological advancement does not create social disparity. When implemented thoughtfully, eco-smart cities promise a vibrant, sustainable, and inclusive future for all urban inhabitants.",
