      "audioScript": "🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 1 (Hội thoại - 1 Giọng Nam, 1 Giọng Nữ):\nTom (Giọng Nam):\tHi Mai! Where did you go last weekend with your class?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tHello Tom! We had a wonderful field trip to Bat Trang pottery village near Ha Noi.\nTom (Giọng Nam):\tBat Trang? That sounds exciting! Did you try making any pottery yourself?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tYes! A local artisan guided us on how to mold wet clay on a spinning wheel to make a small bowl.\nTom (Giọng Nam):\tWas it difficult to shape the clay?\nMai (Giọng Nữ):\tIt required patience and steady hands, but it was so much fun. Crafting pottery helped me unwind and appreciate traditional handicrafts.\n\n🎧 Transcript bài nghe Part 2 (Độc thoại):\nDa Nang is widely celebrated as one of the most livable, modern, and beautiful cities in Viet Nam. Situated along the scenic central coast, the city combines stunning natural landscapes such as the Marble Mountains and Son Tra Peninsula with modern public infrastructure. The local government maintains clean streets, efficient electric bus transit, and beautiful sandy beaches. Furthermore, iconic landmarks like the Dragon Bridge, which breathes fire and water on weekend evenings, make Da Nang an attractive destination for visitors.",
      "writingRubric": "1. Mở đoạn (Topic sentence): 0.25đ\n2. Phát triển ý (Supporting sentences): 0.25đ\n3. Vốn từ vựng & cấu trúc ngữ pháp phong phú: 0.25đ\n4. Độ chính xác chính tả & ngữ pháp: 0.25đ. Tổng: 1.0 điểm.",
      "sampleWritingText": "Preserving traditional craft villages is of great importance for our cultural heritage. Bat Trang pottery village and Van Phuc silk village are vivid symbols of Vietnamese craftsmanship and history. Traditional crafts provide stable livelihoods for local artisans and attract tourists from all over the world. We should support local craft products and introduce them to international friends.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nAcross Viet Nam, numerous traditional craft villages have flourished for hundreds of years. In these communities, skilled artisans (23) ________ their ancestral expertise and secrets down through consecutive generations. Hand-woven conical hats, intricate lacquerware, and hand-molded ceramics are not only artistic creations (24) ________ also cultural symbols reflecting national identity. In recent decades, however, many craft workshops have struggled to compete against mass-produced factory merchandise. To survive, creative villagers have begun adopting digital platforms to (25) ________ their handicrafts to global customers. Furthermore, developing experiential tourism allows travelers to try making items by hand, which brings extra (26) ________ for local households. Protecting these venerable craft villages is vital because they preserve historical heritage and strengthen communal (27) ________ among residents.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nNestled comfortably beside the Red River roughly thirteen kilometers southeast of Hanoi's center, Bat Trang Ceramic Village boasts a rich history spanning over seven centuries. Founded during the Ly Dynasty, this renowned village has long been celebrated across Southeast Asia for its exquisite porcelain and ceramic products, ranging from ceremonial bowls and vases to ornate decorative pottery. What sets Bat Trang ceramics apart is the extraordinary dedication of its local artisans. The production process involves multiple intricate stages: preparing high-grade white clay, shaping pieces on revolving potter's wheels, applying glaze formulas handed down through family lines, and firing the pottery in traditional kilns at temperatures exceeding 1,200 degrees Celsius. In recent years, young craftspeople in Bat Trang have creatively blended timeless motifs with contemporary minimalist designs, captivating modern buyers and foreign tourists alike. Today, Bat Trang is not merely a manufacturing hub; it has transformed into a vibrant cultural destination. Visitors can explore narrow village alleys, visit ancient family kilns, and participate in pottery-making workshops where they shape their own clay souvenirs under an artisan's patient guidance. By continually reinventing their ancestral art, Bat Trang residents have successfully safeguarded their heritage while securing prosperous livelihoods for generations to come.",
