          "explanation": "💡 Đáp án đúng: C (visitors). Thông tin được nêu rõ ràng trong văn bản đọc hiểu.",
          "passage": "Nestled comfortably beside the Red River roughly thirteen kilometers southeast of Hanoi's center, Bat Trang Ceramic Village boasts a rich history spanning over seven centuries. Founded during the Ly Dynasty, this renowned village has long been celebrated across Southeast Asia for its exquisite porcelain and ceramic products, ranging from ceremonial bowls and vases to ornate decorative pottery. What sets Bat Trang ceramics apart is the extraordinary dedication of its local artisans. The production process involves multiple intricate stages: preparing high-grade white clay, shaping pieces on revolving potter's wheels, applying glaze formulas handed down through family lines, and firing the pottery in traditional kilns at temperatures exceeding 1,200 degrees Celsius. In recent years, young craftspeople in Bat Trang have creatively blended timeless motifs with contemporary minimalist designs, captivating modern buyers and foreign tourists alike. Today, Bat Trang is not merely a manufacturing hub; it has transformed into a vibrant cultural destination. Visitors can explore narrow village alleys, visit ancient family kilns, and participate in pottery-making workshops where they shape their own clay souvenirs under an artisan's patient guidance. By continually reinventing their ancestral art, Bat Trang residents have successfully safeguarded their heritage while securing prosperous livelihoods for generations to come."
